ID Task Acceptance criteria Depends on DJ-1 Migration <code>sql/202610190002-create-scheduled-job.sql</code> (table + 6 seed rows per ADR D1), entity <code>ScheduledJob</code>, <code>ScheduledJobRepository</code> Columns and types match ADR D1. The seed holds 6 rows whose cron/zone equal today's annotations; <code>log-stats</code> is <code>0 */5 * * * *</code> and <code>cleanup-old-videos</code> has <code>enabled=false</code>. Every seeded cron passes <code>CronExpression.isValidExpression</code> (a unit test reads the SQL file from the classpath and checks each seeded cron), and every seeded name exists in <code>JobRegistry</code>. No <code>ddl-auto</code> change — DJ-2 <code>jobs/JobRegistry</code> (name constants → <code>AppScheduler</code> method refs) + <code>jobs/DynamicJobScheduler</code> (ADR D3); remove <code>@Scheduled</code> from the 6 methods; drop the wrong log text at <code>:71</code> and the comment at <code>:91</code> Tests (Mockito, mocked <code>TaskScheduler</code>): (a) startup schedules only enabled rows that have code, and WARNs for unknown rows and for code without a row; (b) <code>reschedule</code> cancels the old future before scheduling a new one, and a disabled job ends with no future; (c) a run while one is in progress is skipped (<code>AtomicBoolean</code> guard), and the guard is released after an exception; (d) an exception in a job is caught and recorded as <code>lastResult=FAILED</code>; (e) if loading rows at startup throws, or returns no rows, an ERROR is logged and the app keeps starting. No <code>synchronized</code> (grep). <code>AppSchedulerTest</code> keeps all body tests; only the annotation asserts <code>:326-334</code> are removed DJ-1 DJ-3 <code>service/ScheduledJobService</code> + impl, DTOs <code>ScheduledJobDto</code> / <code>UpdateScheduledJobRequest</code>, <code>web/AdminJobController</code> (GET list, PATCH <code>{name}</code>, POST <code>{name}/runs</code>, ADR D4); i18n error keys en + vi Service tests: an invalid cron gives 400 <code>error.job.invalidCron</code>; a seconds field other than one number (e.g. <code>*/5 * * * * *</code>) gives 400 <code>error.job.tooFrequent</code>; a bad zone gives 400 <code>error.job.invalidZone</code>; an unknown name gives 404 <code>error.job.notFound</code>; a valid PATCH saves first, then calls <code>reschedule</code> (if <code>reschedule</code> throws, the transaction rolls back, so the DB and the live schedule stay the same); PATCH semantics are as follows: <pre><code>- only fields that are sent change;
- `zone: ""` clears it to NULL;
- an empty body gives 400 `error.job.emptyUpdate`;
- `cron` longer than 64 characters gives 400 `error.job.invalidCron`.

Run-now goes through `TaskScheduler.schedule(task, Instant.now())` and returns 202 when started. It works on a disabled job (a manual run), and returns 409 `error.job.running` when the guard is held; `nextRunAt` is null when disabled. `@WebMvcTest` permission test: an ADMIN gets 200 on GET and 403 on PATCH/POST, and a SUPER_ADMIN gets 200/202. `mvn verify` is green with coverage ≥ `api/.coverage-threshold` | DJ-2 |
</code></pre> <p>| DJ-4 | FE <code>api/admin.js</code> (<code>getJobs</code>, <code>updateJob</code>, <code>runJob</code>) + hooks <code>useAdminJobs</code>, <code>useUpdateJob</code>, <code>useRunJob</code> (key <code>['admin','jobs']</code>, mutations invalidate it) | <code>admin.test.js</code>: correct URL/method/body for each call. The hook test shows a mutation success invalidates <code>['admin','jobs']</code> | DJ-3 (API contract) | | DJ-5 | FE <code>components/admin/AdminJobsTab.jsx</code> + <code>SCHEDULED_JOBS</code> in <code>TABS</code>/<code>TAB_QUERY</code>/switch of <code>AdminView.jsx</code> + <code>tabs.SCHEDULED_JOBS</code> and <code>jobs.*</code> keys in en/vi <code>admin.json</code> | Tests (vi + en): the table shows name, description, cron, zone, enabled, next run, last run/result. ADMIN sees read-only (no input or buttons). SUPER_ADMIN can toggle enabled, edit cron (save → <code>updateJob</code> with the new value) and click "Run now" (button disabled while running/pending). A server error key is shown translated. <code>npm run test</code> and <code>npm run lint</code> are green | DJ-4 |</p> <p>Landing: add the feature to <code>docs/tracking.md</code> (it has an ADR and a plan).</p> <p>Commits: BE (DJ-1..3) and FE (DJ-4..5) are 2 commits, each independently mergeable. The FE tab only calls endpoints that exist after the BE commit. Estimate: about 350 LOC BE prod + 300 test, and about 200 LOC FE prod + 150 test.</p>

